 ],
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 6.96,
   "text": "the planet we are missing. The most common planet in our galaxy is one we don't have."
  },
  {
   "start": 7.48,
   "end": 14.84,
   "text": "Not Mercury, not Jupiter, not Earth. Something in between. Scientists call it a super-Earth."
  },
  {
   "start": 15.34,
   "end": 21.56,
   "text": "No, it doesn't wear a cape. So today, we're going to find one. Luna, grab your helmet."
  },
  {
   "start": 21.98,
   "end": 29.16,
   "text": "Let's go on an adventure! So what exactly is a super-Earth? It is a planet bigger than Earth,"
  },
  {
   "start": 29.16,
   "end": 34.66,
   "text": "but smaller than Neptune. Some are rocky, some may be covered in deep oceans."
  },
  {
   "start": 35.58,
   "end": 40.28,
   "text": "Here's the strange part. When scientists started finding planets around other stars,"
  },
  {
   "start": 40.66,
   "end": 47.48,
   "text": "they kept finding super-Earths. Again and again. It is the most common kind of planet found so far."
  },
  {
   "start": 48.04,
   "end": 54.08,
   "text": "But in our solar system, there are none. We got small planets, we got giant planets,"
  },
  {
   "start": 54.08,
   "end": 59.3,
   "text": "but no medium. It's like ordering fries and they ran out of medium."
  },
  {
   "start": 60.16,
   "end": 64.8,
   "text": "Okay Luna, let's land on one. Careful! The gravity here is strong!"
  },
  {
   "start": 65.68,
   "end": 70.94,
   "text": "A super-Earth can be much heavier than our planet. On some, you could feel twice as heavy."
  },
  {
   "start": 71.5,
   "end": 76.3,
   "text": "So if your weighing scale gives you a scary number, don't blame the scale."
  },
  {
   "start": 76.8,
   "end": 80.24,
   "text": "Blame the planet. Every staircase would be leg day."
  },
  {
   "start": 80.24,
   "end": 87.32,
   "text": "Come on Luna, let's visit a few more. First, 55 Cancri E. It is so close to its"
  },
  {
   "start": 87.32,
   "end": 93.54,
   "text": "star that its surface may be covered in lava. Watch your step Luna. Not a great place for"
  },
  {
   "start": 93.54,
   "end": 101.66,
   "text": "a beach holiday. Unless you like your feet extra crispy. Next, LHS 1140B. Not too hot,"
  },
  {
   "start": 102.06,
   "end": 107.82,
   "text": "not too cold. Scientists think it might be an ice world. Maybe with an ocean of liquid water"
  },
  {
   "start": 107.82,
   "end": 116.06,
   "text": "under the ice. Bring a jacket Luna. Actually, bring 10. And now, our last stop. K2-18B."
  },
  {
   "start": 116.74,
   "end": 123.44,
   "text": "Some scientists think it could be a giant ocean world. In 2025, a team reported a possible hint"
  },
  {
   "start": 123.44,
   "end": 130.26,
   "text": "of a gas that, on Earth, is made by living things. Let's take a closer look. Luna, dive in."
  },
  {
   "start": 130.9,
   "end": 137.76,
   "text": "Slowly. It's dark down here. Very quiet. Wait, did you see that? Something is moving."
  },
  {
   "start": 138.46,
   "end": 145.6,
   "text": "Something big. Luna, don't move. It's looking at us. Run Luna! Back to the spaceship! Go, go, go!"
  },
  {
   "start": 147.5,
   "end": 154.12,
   "text": "That was close. Okay, let's be honest. That creature was only our imagination."
  },
  {
   "start": 155.0,
   "end": 158.16,
   "text": "Many scientists say the evidence for life there is still weak."
  },
  {
   "start": 158.16,
   "end": 165.22,
   "text": "Nobody has found life on these planets. Not yet. But scientists are still looking. Think about it."
  },
  {
   "start": 165.5,
   "end": 171.22,
   "text": "The most common planet out there is the one we don't even have. Which means our solar system"
  },
  {
   "start": 171.22,
   "end": 177.8,
   "text": "might be the unusual one. And Earth might be rarer than we ever imagined. And here's the thing."
  },
  {
   "start": 178.64,
   "end": 185.2,
   "text": "Billions of planets, and not one of them, can care. But you can. Don't ever forget how"
  },
  {
   "start": 185.2,
   "end": 191.34,
   "text": "special that makes you. Space is truly amazing. And this is only the beginning."
  }
 ]
}